<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 md:px-6 pb-20 md:pb-28">
  <div class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-forest-200 bg-forest-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-forest-700 mb-6">Avatar Mountains</div>
  <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-900 leading-tight">Avatar Hallelujah Mountain</h1>
  <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">The pillar that made it into Avatar draws a crowd, and the crowd is part of the experience now. But there is a window — early morning, before the tour buses arrive — when you can stand at the viewpoint and see what James Cameron's team saw. It is 1,080 meters of quartz-sandstone, and with mist around the base it genuinely looks like it belongs on another planet.</p>
